<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Haldighati</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1576</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Haldighati was fought on 18 June 1576 in a mountain pass near Gogunda in Mewar between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana-pratap">Maharana Pratap</a> and a Mughal army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/man-singh-i">Man Singh I</a> of Amber for the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> won the field, but Pratap escaped, according to tradition on his horse Chetak, and continued his resistance from the hills. The battle became a lasting symbol of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> defiance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-haldighati.jpg" alt="Battle of Haldighati" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chokha · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chokha,_Battle_of_Haldighati,_painted_1822.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
